blocks:
  - type: metin
    baslik: The difference between sadness and depression
    metin: |-
      Sadness is usually a temporary emotion triggered by a specific event — a loss, disappointment or failure. It eases with time and support, and the person retains some enjoyment of life.

      Depression is different: the low mood does not lift, it persists without a clear cause or out of proportion to circumstances, and the person can no longer enjoy things they once found pleasurable. This disrupts everyday functioning.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: 'DSM-5 diagnostic criterion: the two-week rule'
    metin: A diagnosis of Major Depressive Disorder requires that at least five of the symptoms listed below are present nearly every day for an uninterrupted period of two weeks. One of those symptoms must be either depressed mood or loss of interest or pleasure.
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: Symptoms of depression
    kolon: 3
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Emotional
        maddeler:
          - Persistent sadness or emptiness
          - Loss of interest or pleasure
          - Feelings of worthlessness
          - Excessive guilt
          - Hopelessness, helplessness
          - Thoughts of death or suicide
      - baslik: Cognitive
        maddeler:
          - Difficulty concentrating
          - Trouble making decisions
          - Negative thought patterns
          - Memory problems
          - Self-criticism
      - baslik: Physical
        maddeler:
          - Sleep changes (too much or too little)
          - Appetite changes
          - Fatigue, loss of energy
          - Psychomotor slowing
          - Unexplained aches and pains
  - type: kart-yigini
    baslik: Types of depression
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Major Depressive Disorder
        metin: The most widely recognised type. Symptoms last at least two weeks and significantly impair daily functioning. Episodes may recur.
      - baslik: Dysthymia (Persistent Depressive Disorder)
        metin: A milder but chronic form of depression lasting at least two years. The feeling of "I've always been this way" is common.
      - baslik: Seasonal Affective Disorder
        metin: Begins in autumn–winter and resolves in spring. More prevalent in northern countries and regions with limited sunlight.
      - baslik: Postpartum Depression
        metin: Develops after childbirth and is far more severe and prolonged than the "baby blues". It affects approximately 10–15% of mothers.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: Global scale
    metin: According to the World Health Organisation, approximately 280 million people worldwide are living with depression, making it one of the most prevalent mental health conditions globally. (WHO, 2023)
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: Causes
    giris: 'Depression cannot be attributed to a single cause. It is understood within a biopsychosocial model:'
    kolon: 3
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Biological
        maddeler:
          - Genetic predisposition
          - Serotonin and dopamine imbalances
          - Thyroid and hormonal issues
          - Chronic illness
      - baslik: Psychological
        maddeler:
          - Negative thought schemas
          - Low self-efficacy
          - Past trauma or losses
          - Perfectionism
      - baslik: Social
        maddeler:
          - Loneliness, isolation
          - Relationship difficulties
          - Work or financial stress
          - Weak support network
  - type: onayli-liste
    baslik: Treatment options
    giris: 'Depression is a condition that can largely be overcome with the right support. The main evidence-based approaches include:'
    maddeler:
      - baslik: Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)
        aciklama: Focuses on identifying and changing the negative thought patterns that fuel depression. CBT has the broadest research base of any therapy approach for treating depression.
      - baslik: Antidepressant Medication
        aciklama: Prescribed following [psychiatric evaluation](/en/blog/psychologist-or-psychiatrist.html). For moderate to severe depression, combining medication with therapy generally yields the best outcomes.
      - baslik: Trauma-Focused Therapy
        aciklama: Addresses underlying traumatic experiences to support long-term recovery from depression.
      - baslik: Lifestyle Changes
        aciklama: Regular exercise, sleep hygiene and social connection are important factors that support the treatment process.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: turuncu
    baslik: If you are having thoughts of harming yourself or others
    metin: Please contact a healthcare provider or someone you trust immediately. These thoughts are a symptom of depression and can improve with help.
